+# Agent Note: Chat workspace-file open waterfall
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-05-chat-workspace-file-open-waterfall.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Chat exposes one `ChatViewInjected.openFile` callback to tool rows, produced-file links, and closing-message mentions. The callback directly invoked the native Host opener, so a Client plugin could not present the file itself without replacing Chat presentation code or adding a second file-open registry.
+
+## Decision
+
+The public `/client` helper `openWorkspaceFile(ctx, request)` dispatches the typed `chat/open-workspace-file` waterfall for file paths. `ChatViewInjected.openFile` uses this helper with `preview: true`; external Client callers pass their own preview and placement intent. The request carries the addressed `SessionId`, workspace path, optional preview flag, relative or explicit group target, and opening mode. A listener handles the request by returning without `next()` and delegates by returning `next()`; one request therefore reaches either the handling listener or the terminal native action, never both.
+
+The terminal action preserves the native behavior: it resolves the path with `resolveWorkspacePath(cwd, path)`, calls `session/openWorkspacePath`, and rejects on a Remote refusal. Listener throws and rejections also propagate unchanged to Chat's busy, retry, and stale-settlement handling. The Produced Files **Show in folder** action passes `.` through the same waterfall ([resource display decision](2026-09-05-chat-async-text-links.md)).
+
+Explicit system mode and the optional `workspaceFileOpenPolicy` service's system mode bypass the waterfall and use the native action. The helper reads policy at each call; an absent provider preserves default dispatch. This lets deployment policy apply independently of text-link decoration. The event and policy types belong to ui-chat and name no viewer implementation. An external Client plugin can depend on the exported request type and register an ordinary Cordis listener; ui-chat has no dependency on that plugin.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Add a file-viewer registry.** Rejected because Cordis already provides ordered, disposable middleware and the public helper supplies one file-open entry point for Client consumers.
+
+**Always open natively and notify viewers afterward.** Rejected because it double-opens handled files and gives a viewer no way to replace the native action.
+
+**Catch listener failures and fall back to native opening.** Rejected because an unexpected viewer failure would open a second application and hide the failure from Chat's existing retry UI.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Client plugins can replace file opening per request or delegate to the native Host behavior. Focused ui-chat tests pin native fallback, handled short-circuiting, explicit delegation, request identity, error propagation, and the workspace-folder waterfall. The tool-row file-open decision remains the owner of link presentation and Host opener policy ([tool-call file open](../feature/2026-07-28-tool-call-file-open-in-os.md)).
