+<a id="file-opening"></a>
+## File opening
+
+Chat and external Client plugins open workspace files with the public `openWorkspaceFile(ctx, request)` helper from `/client`. It sends the original request through `chat/open-workspace-file`; Chat supplies `preview: true`, and callers can select preview intent and a relative or explicit group destination. Explicit `mode: 'system'` or the optional `workspaceFileOpenPolicy` service's system mode bypasses handlers. Otherwise a handler returns without `next()` to handle the request or calls `next()` to delegate. The terminal action resolves the path against the Session cwd and calls `session/openWorkspacePath` once. An optional same-process cancellation signal reaches handlers and the native Remote call. Handler and native failures reject without fallback; Chat displays its existing retry dialog ([decision](../../../.agents/notes/implemented/architecture/2026-09-05-chat-workspace-file-open-waterfall.md)).
+
+An optional `ctx.chatTextLinks` provider decorates settled Assistant prose, inline code, authored Markdown destinations, and user/steering/submission bubbles through plain callbacks. Callbacks distinguish prose (`text`), parsed Markdown code spans (`inline-code`), and authored link destinations (`target`). The provider owns resource recognition and opening; Chat preserves logged text, safe external hyperlinks, and existing reference chips. Discovery failures leave ordinary presentation intact. Open failures retain their opaque target in the resource retry dialog. Callbacks read the current provider on each call, so removal cannot invoke a retained provider; newly installed providers take effect on the next text resolution or view mount ([decision](../../../.agents/notes/implemented/architecture/2026-09-05-chat-async-text-links.md)).
